        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="true" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="false" heatedGarage="true" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" evChargingStation="false" outdoorGasAppliances="false" commonSpace="false" elevator="false" fitnessRoom="false" snowmeltSystem="false" unheatedGarage="false" />
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="2" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="1" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>AIR SEALS:

Air leakage have been observed on the following components:

- Windows

- Doors (Arctic entrance)

- Bathroom ceiling fans

- Attic hatch



We recommend:



WOOD WINDOW: The replacement or removal of the wood framed window located in the basement. Since the specified window is located under the entrance porch, it does not have any purpose in terms of light. 

- We recommend closing the opening, re-insulate the section and seal the opening properly.



DOOR: Arctic entrance door seals are not working properly. The infiltration test showed a high level of air leakage at the point of making the interior space cold and uncomfortable.



BATHROOM FANS: 

- We recommend the replacement of the units by more sealed equipment. Also, to ensure the insulation of the evacuation ducts passing in the attic.



ATTIC HATCH: There is air leakage coming from the attic hatch. There also is frosting formation on the interior face of the roof. Since there is an exterior access to the roof, it would be good to think about closing the interior access and seal the section properly.  



AIR SEAL:

We recommend increasing the air tightness of the building by sealing all leaking sections including the all mechanical penetrations through the building envelope.

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>CEILING:

At the moment of the inspection, the roof insulation was R-24. This level of insulation is under the actual territorial standard of R-60.

We recommend the addition of insulation to reach the target of R-60

</ceilings>
                <foundation>FOUNDATION:

During the inspection we noticed an uninsulated section in the basement. This section is located under the wood window.

- We recommend the insulation of the concrete walls. The usage of rigid insulation can insulate well and reduce the effect of thermal bridge. We suggest a material that has the properties of both insulation and vapor barrier. 

</foundation>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the door by an ENERGY STAR certified unit. In the meantime, we suggest the addition of weather strips to increase the air sealing of the door, until you are ready to replace the door.

</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
